# =============================================================================
# Mise-Kal .gitignore
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is aggressive on purpose. Mise-Kal is developed in a private
# workspace and published to a PUBLIC repository, so the cost of a leaked
# credential or a leaked personal note is high and the cost of ignoring one
# extra pattern is zero.
#
# The rule when adding a pattern: if it might ever contain a secret, a personal
# note, an agent instruction or a machine-specific path, ignore it. If it is
# genuinely needed in the repository, add a template instead (see below).

# --- Upstream's own ignores (kept verbatim; do not remove) -------------------
# PocketBase binary is fetched, not vendored
server/bin/
# Live and throwaway databases
server/pb_data/
server/pb_test_data/

# Flutter
app/build/
app/.dart_tool/
app/.flutter-plugins
app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
app/ios/Pods/
app/macos/Pods/

# Build output
installer/out/

.DS_Store
*.log

# Server staged into the app at build time by app/scripts/bundle_server.sh
app/assets/server/

# NOTE: upstream also ignores `.claude/`. That pattern is kept below with the
# rest of the private-tooling rules rather than duplicated here.

# =============================================================================
# SECRETS AND CREDENTIALS
# =============================================================================
# Nothing in this section may ever be committed. Real values live on the
# developer's machine only; the repository carries templates.

# Environment files. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT ignored — it is the
# documented template that says which variables exist, without their values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
!.env.example

# Keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.crt
*.der

# Service account / provider credential files
*credentials*.json
*credential*.json
*service-account*.json
serviceAccount*.json
*secret*.json
*token*.json
!*example*.json

# PocketBase secrets and local admin state
pb_superuser*
*_superuser.json

# Payment provider configuration with real values
config.local.*
*.local.json
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml

# SSH and GPG material
.ssh/
*.pub
!deploy/*.pub

# =============================================================================
# PRIVATE AGENT INSTRUCTIONS AND MEMORY
# =============================================================================
# The repository carries its own public AGENTS.md, which documents how to work
# here. Anything personal — an individual's private prompts, memory, notes to
# themselves, or a local agent configuration — must stay out.

# Agent instruction and memory files that are personal rather than project
.agents/
.cursor/
.codex/
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE.md.bak
*private*.md
*personal*.md
*memory*.md
!README.md

# Specific personal note locations
notes/
private/
.local-notes/

# =============================================================================
# MACHINE-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# These differ per developer and are meaningless to anyone else. Committing them
# causes spurious diffs and, occasionally, leaks a username or an internal path.

# Harness runtime state and local tuning
.harness/worktrees/
.harness/locks/
.harness/logs/
.harness/cache/
.harness/harness.conf

# Editor and IDE state
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS metadata
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# =============================================================================
# BUILD AND TEST ARTEFACTS
# =============================================================================
# Reproducible output. If it can be regenerated, it does not belong in git.

# Dart / Flutter
.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
*.g.dart
*.freezed.dart

# Test and coverage output
coverage/
.test_output/
*.tmp
*.temp

# Flutter's Windows/macOS/Linux build directories
app/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
app/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
app/linux/flutter/ephemeral/

# Server runtime
server/pb_test_data/
server/pb_guest_test_data/
server/pb_*_test_data/
server/pb_data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Logs
logs/
*.log
!docs/**/*.log

# Archives produced during packaging
*.zip
*.dmg
*.msi
*.exe
!app/windows/runner/resources/*.ico

# =============================================================================
# WHAT MUST *NOT* BE IGNORED
# =============================================================================
# Templates are the whole point of the public/private split: they document what
# configuration exists without carrying a value. These are explicitly kept:
#
#   .env.example
#   config.example.*
#   docs/
#   app/pubspec.lock      (lockfiles are committed so builds are reproducible)
#   server/pb_migrations/ (the schema IS the source of truth)
